# Smart Device Management System

## Project Description

This project is a simple Smart Device 
Management System developed using Python. It 
demonstrates the basic concepts of Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), including classes, objects, inheritance, encapsulation, constructors, methods, getters and setters, and 
the use of super(). 

The program manages different smart devices used in a smart home:
- Temperature Sensor
- Smart Light
- Security Camera

Users can interact with the devices through a simple menu-driven interface.

## Features

- Display device information
- Turn devices on and off
- Read temperature from the temperature sensor
- Increase or decrease the smart light brightness
- Start recording with the security camera
- Menu-driven program using loops and conditional statements

## Programming Concepts Used

- Variables and data types
- Input and output
- Conditional statements
- Loops
- Functions (methods)
- Classes and objects
- Constructors ('__init__')
- Inheritance
- Encapsulation
- Getters and setters (@property)
- super()

## Requirements

- Python 3.x
- PyCharm (or any Python IDE)
  
## How to Run the Program

1. Download or clone this repository.
2. Open the project in PyCharm.
3. Run the main.py file.
4. Follow the menu displayed on the screen.

